                <pb facs="0681" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg601"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Jérémie.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of yesterday (May 27) informing me of the formation of a
                    Provisional Government, with General Canal as President, and yourself charged
                    with the functions of minister of foreign relations in the said Government.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
